  "final": "I added `ContactStore.find_by_phone(number)` in `contacts/store.py`. I haven't run it or added tests.\n\nIt normalizes the input with the same `normalize_phone` that `add()` uses on stored numbers. So `\"(415) 555-0100\"`, `\"415-555-0100\"` and `\"+1 415 555 0100\"` all match the same contact. It returns a list of matching contacts, like `find_by_name`.\n\nIf the input isn't a plausible phone number, `normalize_phone` raises `ValueError`, and the method returns `[]` instead of raising. If you'd rather it raise, remove the `try/except`.\n\nI didn't use `clean_phone` in `contacts/compat.py`. It only strips non-digits, so `\"+1 415…\"` and `\"415…\"` would give different results, and stored numbers are in E.164 form.",
